{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only (scvi_n200) achieves 0.520 acc, image-only (resnet50) is very weak at 0.208, and the multimodal model (scvi_n200 + resnet50) barely improves over RNA-only (0.536 vs 0.520). This suggests the resnet50 image encoder is not contributing meaningful signal. The key uncertainty is whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) can make the image modality actually useful in a multimodal setting. config_002 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l relative to config_011, keeping all other settings identical (scvi_n200, singleprofile, concat fusion, no aggregation). This isolates the effect of image encoder quality. If config_002 substantially exceeds config_011, the image modality is worth further investment (multiprofile, aggregation, fusion tuning). If it does not, we can confidently deprioritize image-heavy configurations and focus budget on RNA-side improvements (multiprofile, alternative RNA encoders). This single-variable comparison is the highest-information experiment available for resolving the central design question of whether multimodal fusion is worthwhile."
}

